  notes: "ANDROID defaults (unit: dp = 1/160 inch).\n\nSOURCE: AOSP ViewConfiguration
    / GestureDetector defaults. Used when the OS values cannot be read (e.g. in the
    Editor).\n\nREPLACED AT RUNTIME by the device's own values when policy.useOsValues
    is on (includes the user's accessibility settings): touchSlopDp, doubleTapSlopDp,
    edgeSlopDp, minScalingSpanDp (API 29+), minFlingVelocityDps, maxFlingVelocityDps,
    longPressTimeoutMs, doubleTapTimeoutMs. Density always comes from DisplayMetrics.densityDpi.\n\nminScalingSpanDp
    170 = AOSP config_minScalingSpan (27 mm).\nlongPressTimeoutMs 400 = current AOSP
    default (older Android versions used 500).\n\nGUESSES - check on real devices (plan.md
    Q2):\n- fallbackDpi 420: typical modern phone.\n- multiFingerTapWindowMs 150.\n-
    velocityWindowMs 100: similar to Android's VelocityTracker horizon.\n- swipeAngleToleranceDeg
    30.\n- minRotationDeg 5."
